test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T06:42:43.4480968Z             "body": "Preserves original Playwright MCP tools and adds a bounded local batch/jobs companion. Publishing remains disabled. **Draft; not release-ready.**\n\nLatest completed native78 at `92c626108ad59c80cd2f814dc064d3a0c34f4499`: **1,907 reported test passes / 6 failures**, plus Mac actual-Codex TIMED_OUT928 and two failed Windows diagnostic JSON controls. [Batch QA](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39732651064):1,448/4; [original CI](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39732651058):459/2. Both workflows fail. All17 non-soak jobs conclude; optional soak skips; reported test skips/cancellations0.\n\nAllLinux batch and four journal lanes pass. Five175-file production installs, five strict ownership units,15 all-action fixtures,15 cancellation cases (60 scenarios), five supervised and five raw20-screenshot fixtures pass. Both instrumented Windows jobs tests pass; their new failure paths are unexercised and do not explain native77 journal RPC/connection failures.\n\nRemaining test failures: Mac raw995 timeout and SDKall1,000 actions but lifecycle TIMED_OUT; Windows headed Firefox completes23 then server-close/kill timeout, and Firefox429 sees2GET/2finished but0navigation acknowledgements; Mac original screenshot protocol capture error; Windows legacy headless sixth run14/23 locator timeout. Normal Windows/Linux original suites152 each pass. Mac modal follow-up and later runs/scenarios inside failed cases remain unexecuted. Linux/Windows actual-Codex1k pass with model0/owned0, Mac928 fails with known terminated/removed cleanup and no guardian/journal fault facts.\n\nSeparate private-temp Firefox4/10 and protocol-headed2/10 controls fail despite zero observed residuals; inherited/stock-headed10/10 pass. Healthy later Mac transport controls do not establish a causal fix. Full legacy rows/birth ledgers retained; one candidate has a different recorded PID incarnation, while older unclassified observations/debt remain unresolved.\n\nLocal follow-up only records captured/exitObserved booleans from the existing Firefox adapter’s actual public ChildProcess handle when a raw run fails. No added query/wait/signal/kill authority, failure-status change or deadline change. Existing Linux Firefox23-action case passes once eachNode20/22/24; new failure branch unexercised. Lint/diff and175-file dry pack pass. Runtime source remains9591621. Native verification of this diagnostic is next.\n\nAll17 ordinary per-job logs and EOF retry receipt saved under docs/evidence/worker-ci-seventyeighth-* and native78-*. No artifact downloads, auth/TLS workaround, deadline raises, forced/replayed input, default transport/channel changes or PID-based debt clearance. Remaining failed G00–G18 gates and unsupported scope are explicit in the execution ledger/report. No merge or release requested.\n",
